# WN22-DC-000020: Windows Server 2022 Kerberos user logon restrictions must be enforced.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-dc-000020-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 Kerberos user logon restrictions must be enforced.`
    description `This policy setting determines whether the Kerberos Key Distribution Center (KDC) validates every request for a session ticket against the user rights policy of the target computer. The policy is enabled by default, which is the most secure setting for validating that access to target resources is not circumvented. Satisfies: SRG-OS-000112-GPOS-00057, SRG-OS-000113-GPOS-00058`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,medium,kerberos-policy,security-policy,ksi-iam-apm,ksi-iam-mfa`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-IAM-APM,KSI:KSI-IAM-MFA,NIST-800-53:IA-2(8)`
    control_objective `KSI-IAM-APM,KSI-IAM-MFA`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value in the Default Domain Policy for Computer Configuration >> Policies >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Account Policies >> Kerberos Policy >> Enforce user logon restrictions to "Enabled".`

    component_id `comp-windows-security-policy`

    impl_KSI_IAM_APM `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-APM by enforcing TicketValidateClient per the STIG (Kerberos user logon restrictions must be enforced (TicketValidateClient = 1).). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_KSI_IAM_MFA `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-MFA by enforcing TicketValidateClient per the STIG (Kerberos user logon restrictions must be enforced (TicketValidateClient = 1).). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_IA_2_8 `Windows Server implements IA-2(8) by enforcing TicketValidateClient per the STIG (Kerberos user logon restrictions must be enforced (TicketValidateClient = 1).). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        policy_name `TicketValidateClient`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value_int int = 1
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN windows_security_policy
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
